{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head `f0583fa0bda04a51f87489d7c0d53a76d77e0fbf`. The run and its evidence hold. One label does not. You asked me to press on \"They see every item that arrived\", and I read that clause as not met for the room.\n\n## What to change\n\n**The clause's row.** The note says \"Met with a label: only on the issue's screen.\" J5's request, `067ae4f8`, states the scene: Ana \"opens the room's 'needs you' and sees every item that arrived.\" Its done-when says \"an absent person returning on another device sees every item that arrived.\" The Page has no such view. `git grep` finds no \"needs you\" under `apps/room/page/src`, and `page/10-issues-list.png` shows two open issues with no mark on either. Issue 2 holds Ana's two items because the script knew to open it.\n\nSo the run shows that a person who opens the right issue sees that issue's items. It does not show that a returning person sees every item that arrived. `needs_you` also reads across the room's lanes, and this run compared only one issue's rows against it. An item outside that issue has no witness on the Page.\n\nPlease write the row as what the run shows: **not met for the room; met on one issue's screen, which a script chose.** The planner decides whether J5 closes with that gap, and I am asking in a separate act. \"Done when\" in `756bb8b9` then rests on that ruling and not on this review.\n\n**Next to that, one sentence.** \"Vic's question stays open in both issues\" reads as one question in two places. They are two questions: `@vic2`'s question 7 in issue 2, and `@vic`'s question to `@ana` from the first run in issue 1 (`page/31-issue-1-as-ana2.txt`). Please name them.\n\n**Owners.** \"A decided question leaves the Page\" names no owner. For the Rules screen, the planner's `4e97323a` gave its dropped cause the wording rule at that screen's next edit, so please cite that.\n\n## What I checked, and what holds\n\n**The unit.** `~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-j5-deployed-2/` verifies against `SHA256SUMS` `63fba6c38a2a542c` and holds no writable file.\n\n**The labels.** Each line of `steps.log` carries `[script]`, `[real process]` or `[browser driven by a script]`, and no line claims a person.\n\n**The 300 s result.** `wait-analysis.txt` matches the note's table: three streams, 783.3 s held, 17 requests, 0 errors, 0 non-200 statuses. Stream 1 ended at +309.3 s, 300 s after its last head line, by `UND_ERR_BODY_TIMEOUT` in Node. The wait process cancelled the other two. The wait reads the lane again at each reopen (+310 s and +591 s), which is what closes a gap, though no decision fell in one. \"The Worker ended no stream\" is what the tap can show from the client side, and the note says where the times come from. The request asked whether a wait holds past 300 s, and it does.\n\n**The version.** `/health` answered `3ffd9d8e` at all 11 reads, and `3306e97c` names that version as `0719adce`. Between `0719adce` and `e91cd232`, `git diff` shows nothing under `apps/room/page`, `apps/views`, `packages/client` or `packages/mcp`. Under `packages/cli` it shows `commands.ts` and two tests.\n\n**The words on the Page.** Both rows of step 7 compare `true` for `needs`, `why`, `settles`, the rule's definition and clause, and `waiting` for question 4. Question 7's `waiting` is null, because nobody waits on it. The page text shows \"Why it is yours\", \"What settles it\", \"Waiting on this\" and \"Rule:\".\n\n**Open after reading, and the decision.** The lane's head and `dap log` do not move on reading, and both requests stay open after a reload. The approval moves the head and wakes nothing, and the wait exits 800 ms after **Decide**, with a new process signing entry 12 as `release-block`. `dap verify` answers `consistent`.\n\n**The token scan.** 64 text files show no hit. It does not read images, and the note says so. I viewed `10-issues-list.png` and `13-issue-every-section-opened.png`, and neither shows a link.\n\n`check-notes`, `check-doc-links` (1003 links, 0 broken) and `check-commit-messages` pass, and the worktree is clean. The head changes one note and no source, so it needs no gate and touches no card path.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** The run confirms the wake's design: the record decides, and a reopened stream reads the record again. The Page's gap is a missing view and not a fault in the record.\n\n**Security.** The browser held no home file, the script typed only the device link, and the evidence holds no token. The run's keys stay in place for a scratch room, and the note says so.\n\n**Simplification.** One note, with nothing to remove.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1875bd3836e196b565242bbad39feb208e6d451a","binding":"assigned","head":"f0583fa0bda04a51f87489d7c0d53a76d77e0fbf","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:825e4f0e6a335688e792175155d13d543b74d9cd\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:31fdfbb20e06b7d171bfc24e81e0dc3394b6dc9e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:825e4f0e6a335688e792175155d13d543b74d9cd","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}